From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Lawler <patricktlawler@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 17:20:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: qcom_q6v5_wcss: use the BE550 IPQ9574 support

Replace the IPQ9574 support from the previous patches with the version
tested on the TP-Link Archer BE550. Compared to them, it:

- checks the Q6SS boot status (polled every 1 ms for up to 20 ms), and
  asserts the AON reset and disables the clocks again when
  q6v7_wcss_reset() or the start fails
- waits up to 1 s for SSCAON_STATUS in q6v7_wcss_powerdown()
  (HALT_CHECK_MAX_LOOPS is a loop count, not a timeout in microseconds)
- writes the boot address for QCS404 and IPQ8074 again
- asserts the Q6 reset before the WCSS reset when powering the Q6 down
- only ignores a missing M3 firmware and returns other load errors
- adds a per-SoC auto_boot flag, off for IPQ9574: ath11k boots the Q6
  through qcom,rproc, and booting it at probe with the driver built in
  requests the firmware before the root filesystem is mounted
- loads the Q6 and M3 firmware from ath11k/IPQ9574/hw1.0/
- keeps the QCS404 clocks, the resets and the reserved memory lookup
  as in Linux 6.18
- uses named bits for the CBCR enable and the clock source mux, and
  fixes the TCSR_GLOBAL_CFG1 error message

Signed-off-by: Patrick Lawler <patricktlawler@gmail.com>
